  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#M1010">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#Mitigation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Deploy Compromised Device Detection Method</rdfs:label>
    <riskonto:description>A variety of methods exist that can be used to enable enterprises to identify compromised (e.g. rooted/jailbroken) devices, whether using security mechanisms built directly into the device, third-party mobile security applications, enterprise mobility management (EMM)/mobile device management (MDM) capabilities, or other methods. Some methods may be trivial to evade while others may be more sophisticated.</riskonto:description>
