Adversaries may use ARP cache poisoning as a means to intercept network traffic. This activity may be used to collect and/or relay data such as credentials, especially those sent over an insecure, unencrypted protocol.(Citation: Sans ARP Spoofing Aug 2003)</rdfs:comment>
    <riskonto:techniqueID>T1557.002</riskonto:techniqueID>
