  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#M0932">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#Mitigation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Multi-factor Authentication</rdfs:label>
    <riskonto:description>Use two or more pieces of evidence to authenticate to a system; such as username and password in addition to a token from a physical smart card or token generator.  Within industrial control environments assets such as low-level controllers, workstations, and HMIs have real-time operational control and safety requirements which may restrict the use of multi-factor.</riskonto:description>
    <rdfs:comment>Use two or more pieces of evidence to authenticate to a system; such as username and password in addition to a token from a physical smart card or token generator.  Within industrial control environments assets such as low-level controllers, workstations, and HMIs have real-time operational control and safety requirements which may restrict the use of multi-factor.</rdfs:comment>
    <riskonto:mitigationID>M0932</riskonto:mitigationID>
    <riskonto:externalID>M0932</riskonto:externalID>
  </rdf:Description>
