  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#T0870">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#AttackTechnique"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#ICSTechnique"/>
    <rdfs:label>Detect Program State</rdfs:label>
    <riskonto:description>Adversaries may seek to gather information about the current state of a program on a PLC. State information reveals information about the program, including whether it's running, halted, stopped, or has generated an exception. This information may be leveraged as a verification of malicious program execution or to determine if a PLC is ready to download a new program.</riskonto:description>
    <rdfs:comment>Adversaries may seek to gather information about the current state of a program on a PLC. State information reveals information about the program, including whether it's running, halted, stopped, or has generated an exception. This information may be leveraged as a verification of malicious program execution or to determine if a PLC is ready to download a new program.</rdfs:comment>
    <riskonto:techniqueID>T0870</riskonto:techniqueID>
    <riskonto:externalID>T0870</riskonto:externalID>
    <riskonto:platform>ics</riskonto:platform>
    <riskonto:mitigatedBy rdf:resource="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#M0800"/>
    <riskonto:mitigatedBy rdf:resource="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#M0801"/>
