  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#T1126">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#AttackTechnique"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cs.unb.ca/ontologies/riskonto#EnterpriseTechnique"/>
    <rdfs:label>Network Share Connection Removal</rdfs:label>
    <riskonto:description>Adversaries may remove share connections that are no longer useful in order to clean up traces of their operation. Windows shared drive and [Windows Admin Shares](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1077) connections can be removed when no longer needed. [Net](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0039) is an example utility that can be used to remove network share connections with the &lt;code&gt;net use \\system\share /delete&lt;/code&gt; command. (Citation: Technet Net Use)</riskonto:description>
    <rdfs:comment>Adversaries may remove share connections that are no longer useful in order to clean up traces of their operation. Windows shared drive and [Windows Admin Shares](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1077) connections can be removed when no longer needed. [Net](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0039) is an example utility that can be used to remove network share connections with the &lt;code&gt;net use \\system\share /delete&lt;/code&gt; command. (Citation: Technet Net Use)</rdfs:comment>
    <riskonto:techniqueID>T1126</riskonto:techniqueID>
    <riskonto:externalID>T1126</riskonto:externalID>
    <riskonto:platform>enterprise</riskonto:platform>
  </rdf:Description>
