This ensures persistence, as it causes the DLL (in this case, foo.dll) to be loaded each time the Winsock 2 library is invoked.</rdfs:comment>
    <riskonto:techniqueID>T1574.011</riskonto:techniqueID>
    <riskonto:externalID>T1574.011</riskonto:externalID>
